      <p><strong>Optional module.</strong> See <a href="/dogsbay-xml-dita-tutorial-docs/start-here/learning-path">Choose a learning path</a>. <strong>You need:</strong> stage 17 complete. <strong>Time:</strong> about 35 minutes.</p>
      <h2 id="add-the-production-topics" class="group scroll-mt-20">Add the production topics<a href="#add-the-production-topics" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <p>Create the following files. The effects reference and presets use separate source files. Each gets an explicit topicref in the production maps. The effect-order concept supports the reusable cleanup branch. The guide information topic is published in print output.</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"\u003c?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n\u003c!DOCTYPE reference PUBLIC \"-//OASIS//DTD DITA Reference//EN\" \"reference.dtd\">\n\n\u003creference id=\"effects-reference\">\n  \u003ctitle>Effects reference\u003c/title>\n  \u003cshortdesc>The built-in effects, what each one does, and the parameters that matter.\u003c/shortdesc>\n  \u003cprolog>\n    \u003cauthor type=\"creator\">The Audacity tutorial team\u003c/author>\n    \u003ccritdates>\n      \u003ccreated date=\"2026-02-10\"/>\n    \u003c/critdates>\n    \u003cmetadata>\n      \u003caudience type=\"user\"/>\n      \u003ccategory>reference\u003c/category>\n      \u003ckeywords>\n        \u003ckeyword>effects\u003c/keyword>\n        \u003ckeyword>Amplify\u003c/keyword>\n        \u003ckeyword>Compressor\u003c/keyword>\n        \u003ckeyword>Normalize\u003c/keyword>\n        \u003cindexterm>effects\u003cindexterm>reference\u003c/indexterm>\u003c/indexterm>\n      \u003c/keywords>\n    \u003c/metadata>\n  \u003c/prolog>\n  \u003crefbody>\n    \u003csection>\n      \u003cp>\u003ckeyword keyref=\"product-name\"/> includes several built-in effects.\n        Select a region of audio, then choose an effect from the \u003cuicontrol>Effect\u003c/uicontrol> menu.\u003c/p>\n    \u003c/section>\n    \u003ctable outputclass=\"compact\">\n      \u003ctitle>Built-in audio effects\u003c/title>\n      \u003ctgroup cols=\"3\">\n        \u003ccolspec colname=\"effect\" colwidth=\"1*\"/>\n        \u003ccolspec colname=\"description\" colwidth=\"2*\"/>\n        \u003ccolspec colname=\"parameters\" colwidth=\"2*\"/>\n        \u003cthead>\n          \u003crow>\n            \u003centry>Effect\u003c/entry>\n            \u003centry>Description\u003c/entry>\n            \u003centry>Key parameters\u003c/entry>\n          \u003c/row>\n        \u003c/thead>\n        \u003ctbody>\n          \u003crow>\n            \u003centry>Amplify\u003c/entry>\n            \u003centry>Increases or decreases the volume of the selection.\u003c/entry>\n            \u003centry>Amplification (dB); \u003cuicontrol>Allow clipping\u003c/uicontrol>.\u003c/entry>\n          \u003c/row>\n          \u003crow>\n            \u003centry>Noise Reduction\u003c/entry>\n            \u003centry>Removes steady background noise such as hum, hiss or fan noise.\n              Needs a noise profile.\u003c/entry>\n            \u003centry>Noise reduction (dB): 6 to 12 for mild noise, 12 to 24 for heavy; sensitivity; frequency smoothing.\u003c/entry>\n          \u003c/row>\n          \u003crow>\n            \u003centry>Compressor\u003c/entry>\n            \u003centry>Reduces the dynamic range: quiet parts louder, loud parts quieter.\u003c/entry>\n            \u003centry>Threshold (dB), ratio (for example 3:1), attack and release times.\u003c/entry>\n          \u003c/row>\n          \u003crow>\n            \u003centry>Normalize\u003c/entry>\n            \u003centry>Sets the peak amplitude to a target level and optionally removes DC offset.\u003c/entry>\n            \u003centry>Peak amplitude (dB), typically -1.0; \u003cuicontrol>Remove DC offset\u003c/uicontrol>.\u003c/entry>\n          \u003c/row>\n          \u003crow>\n            \u003centry>Fade In, Fade Out\u003c/entry>\n            \u003centry>Ramps the volume of the selection up from silence, or down to it.\u003c/entry>\n            \u003centry>None: a linear fade over the selection.\u003c/entry>\n          \u003c/row>\n        \u003c/tbody>\n      \u003c/tgroup>\n    \u003c/table>\n  \u003c/refbody>\n\u003c/reference>"} lang="xml" title="topics/effects-reference.dita" />
      <CodeBlock code={"\u003c?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n\u003c!DOCTYPE reference PUBLIC \"-//OASIS//DTD DITA Reference//EN\" \"reference.dtd\">\n\n\u003creference id=\"effect-presets\">\n  \u003ctitle>Presets\u003c/title>\n  \u003cshortdesc>Most effect dialogs can save their settings as a named preset.\u003c/shortdesc>\n  \u003cprolog>\n    \u003cauthor type=\"creator\">The Audacity tutorial team\u003c/author>\n    \u003cmetadata>\n      \u003ckeywords>\n        \u003ckeyword>presets\u003c/keyword>\n      \u003c/keywords>\n    \u003c/metadata>\n  \u003c/prolog>\n  \u003crefbody>\n    \u003csection>\n      \u003cp>In an effect dialog, choose \u003cmenucascade>\u003cuicontrol>Presets and settings\u003c/uicontrol>\u003cuicontrol>Save Preset\u003c/uicontrol>\u003c/menucascade> and give the settings a name.\n        The preset then appears in the same menu for that effect in every project.\u003c/p>\n    \u003c/section>\n  \u003c/refbody>\n\u003c/reference>"} lang="xml" title="topics/effect-presets.dita" />
      <CodeBlock code={"\u003c?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n\u003c!DOCTYPE concept PUBLIC \"-//OASIS//DTD DITA Concept//EN\" \"concept.dtd\">\n\n\u003cconcept id=\"effect-order\">\n  \u003ctitle>Why the order of effects matters\u003c/title>\n  \u003cshortdesc>Clean first, then shape: noise reduction before compression, and normalization last.\u003c/shortdesc>\n  \u003cprolog>\n    \u003cauthor type=\"creator\">The Audacity tutorial team\u003c/author>\n    \u003cmetadata>\n      \u003caudience type=\"user\" experiencelevel=\"intermediate\"/>\n      \u003ccategory>concept\u003c/category>\n      \u003ckeywords>\n        \u003ckeyword>effects\u003c/keyword>\n        \u003ckeyword>order\u003c/keyword>\n      \u003c/keywords>\n    \u003c/metadata>\n  \u003c/prolog>\n  \u003cconbody>\n    \u003cp>Every effect works on whatever the previous one left.\n    Compression raises quiet passages, so background noise compressed before it is removed becomes louder and harder to profile.\n    Normalization sets the final peak, so anything applied after it can push the audio into \u003cterm keyref=\"gl-clipping\">clipping\u003c/term>.\u003c/p>\n    \u003cp>A safe order for spoken word: noise reduction, editing, compression, normalization, export.\u003c/p>\n  \u003c/conbody>\n\u003c/concept>"} lang="xml" title="topics/effect-order.dita" />
      <CodeBlock code={"\u003c?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n\u003c!DOCTYPE topic PUBLIC \"-//OASIS//DTD DITA Topic//EN\" \"topic.dtd\">\n\n\u003ctopic id=\"about-this-guide\">\n  \u003ctitle>About this guide\u003c/title>\n  \u003cshortdesc>Who wrote this guide, the licence it is published under, and the material it adapts.\u003c/shortdesc>\n  \u003cprolog>\n    \u003cauthor type=\"creator\">The Audacity tutorial team\u003c/author>\n    \u003cmetadata>\n      \u003caudience type=\"user\"/>\n      \u003ccategory>front matter\u003c/category>\n      \u003ckeywords>\n        \u003ckeyword>licence\u003c/keyword>\n        \u003ckeyword>credits\u003c/keyword>\n      \u003c/keywords>\n    \u003c/metadata>\n  \u003c/prolog>\n  \u003cbody>\n    \u003cp>This guide is published under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 licence.\n    Its topics are adapted from the Audacity Manual, copyright the Audacity Team and the Manual's authors, under the Creative Commons Attribution 3.0 licence.\u003c/p>\n    \u003cp>New to \u003ckeyword keyref=\"product-name\"/>? Start with \u003cxref keyref=\"start-here\"/>.\n    New to audio? Read \u003cxref keyref=\"digital-audio\"/> first.\n    Here for podcasting? Go straight to \u003cxref keyref=\"podcast-workflow\"/>.\u003c/p>\n    \u003cp>\u003ckeyword keyref=\"product-name\"/> is a registered trademark of Dominic Mazzoni.\n    The Audacity Team does not endorse this guide and is not affiliated with it.\u003c/p>\n  \u003c/body>\n\u003c/topic>"} lang="xml" title="topics/about-this-guide.dita" />
      <h2 id="update-the-production-maps" class="group scroll-mt-20">Update the production maps<a href="#update-the-production-maps" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <p>Apply the map changes below. <code>to-content</code> combines the introductory topics. <code>print="printonly"</code> restricts the guide information topic to print output; <code>toc="no"</code> and <code>search="no"</code> control navigation and search where supported.</p>
      <p>The <code>cleanup</code> topicset names a reusable branch. The podcaster map includes that branch with <code>topicsetref</code>. The beginner map uses <code>copy-to</code> to give the audio-formats topic a different output filename.</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/audacity-guide.ditamap\n+++ b/audacity-guide.ditamap\n@@ -28,9 +28,12 @@\n   \u003c!-- Warehouses: pulled in by conref and conkeyref, never pages of their own. -->\n   \u003ckeydef keys=\"common-notes\" href=\"shared/common-notes.dita\"/>\n   \u003ctopicref href=\"shared/common-steps.dita\" processing-role=\"resource-only\"/>\n+  \u003c!-- Print only: the licence page belongs in the PDF, not in the web TOC or search. -->\n+  \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/about-this-guide.dita\" print=\"printonly\" toc=\"no\" search=\"no\"/>\n \n   \u003ctopichead navtitle=\"Getting started\">\n-    \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/what-is-audacity.dita\" collection-type=\"family\">\n+    \u003c!-- Two small topics, one page: to-content merges the child into the parent. -->\n+    \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/what-is-audacity.dita\" collection-type=\"family\" chunk=\"to-content\">\n       \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/what-is-digital-audio.dita\" keys=\"digital-audio\"/>\n     \u003c/topicref>\n     \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/installing-audacity.dita\" keys=\"install\"/>\n@@ -43,7 +46,11 @@\n       \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/trimming-audio.dita\"/>\n       \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/exporting-audio.dita\"/>\n     \u003c/topicgroup>\n-    \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/removing-background-noise.dita\" linking=\"targetonly\"/>\n+    \u003c!-- A topicset: a named, reusable branch other maps can pull in by topicsetref. -->\n+    \u003ctopicset id=\"cleanup\" navtitle=\"Cleaning up a recording\">\n+      \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/removing-background-noise.dita\" linking=\"targetonly\"/>\n+      \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/effect-order.dita\"/>\n+    \u003c/topicset>\n   \u003c/topichead>\n \n   \u003ctopichead navtitle=\"Podcast production\" audience=\"podcaster\">\n@@ -56,6 +63,8 @@\n         \u003cnavtitle>Audio formats\u003c/navtitle>\n       \u003c/topicmeta>\n     \u003c/topicref>\n+    \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/effects-reference.dita\" keys=\"effects\"/>\n+    \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/effect-presets.dita\"/>\n   \u003c/topichead>\n   \u003ctopichead navtitle=\"Glossary\">\n     \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/glossary/audio-units.dita\"/>"} lang="diff" title="audacity-guide.ditamap" />
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/beginner-guide.ditamap\n+++ b/beginner-guide.ditamap\n@@ -21,6 +21,7 @@\n     \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/exporting-audio.dita\"/>\n   \u003c/topichead>\n   \u003ctopichead navtitle=\"Quick reference\">\n-    \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/supported-audio-formats.dita\" keys=\"formats\"/>\n+    \u003c!-- The same source topic, published under a different file name in this guide. -->\n+    \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/supported-audio-formats.dita\" keys=\"formats\" copy-to=\"topics/formats-quick-reference.dita\"/>\n   \u003c/topichead>\n \u003c/map>"} lang="diff" title="beginner-guide.ditamap" />
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/podcaster-guide.ditamap\n+++ b/podcaster-guide.ditamap\n@@ -23,7 +23,7 @@\n     \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/preparing-to-record.dita\"/>\n     \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/recording-your-first-track.dita\"/>\n     \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/trimming-audio.dita\"/>\n-    \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/removing-background-noise.dita\"/>\n+    \u003ctopicsetref href=\"audacity-guide.ditamap#cleanup\"/>\n     \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/exporting-audio.dita\"/>\n   \u003c/topichead>\n   \u003ctopichead navtitle=\"Podcast production\">\n@@ -31,6 +31,8 @@\n   \u003c/topichead>\n   \u003ctopichead navtitle=\"Reference\">\n     \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/supported-audio-formats.dita\" keys=\"formats\"/>\n+    \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/effects-reference.dita\" keys=\"effects\"/>\n+    \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/effect-presets.dita\"/>\n     \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/glossary/audio-units.dita\"/>\n     \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/glossary/g-compression.dita\"/>\n     \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/glossary/g-normalization.dita\"/>"} lang="diff" title="podcaster-guide.ditamap" />
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/topics/podcast-production-workflow.dita\n+++ b/topics/podcast-production-workflow.dita\n@@ -43,7 +43,7 @@\n     \u003c/section>\n     \u003csection audience=\"podcaster\">\n       \u003ctitle>Post-production\u003c/title>\n-      \u003cp>Process the audio in this order:\u003c/p>\n+      \u003cp>Process the audio in this order (see \u003cxref keyref=\"effects\"/> for each effect's parameters):\u003c/p>\n       \u003col>\n         \u003cli>\u003cb>Noise reduction\u003c/b>: remove background noise using the noise profile from the silence.\u003c/li>\n         \u003cli>\u003cb>Editing\u003c/b>: trim mistakes, long pauses and false starts.\u003c/li>"} lang="diff" title="topics/podcast-production-workflow.dita" />
      <h2 id="compare-combined-and-split-pages" class="group scroll-mt-20">Compare combined and split pages<a href="#compare-combined-and-split-pages" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <p>Create these files under <code>examples/chunking/</code>. This example has its own maps and is excluded from the deliverables in <code>project.json</code>.</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"\u003c?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n\u003c!DOCTYPE reference PUBLIC \"-//OASIS//DTD DITA Reference//EN\" \"reference.dtd\">\n\u003creference id=\"chunk-parent\">\n  \u003ctitle>Chunking demonstration\u003c/title>\n  \u003cshortdesc>Compare a combined page with separate pages for nested topics.\u003c/shortdesc>\n  \u003cprolog>\u003cauthor>The tutorial team\u003c/author>\u003cmetadata>\u003ckeywords>\u003ckeyword>chunking\u003c/keyword>\u003c/keywords>\u003c/metadata>\u003c/prolog>\n  \u003crefbody>\u003csection>\u003cp>The parent and child share one source file.\u003c/p>\u003c/section>\u003c/refbody>\n  \u003creference id=\"chunk-child\">\n    \u003ctitle>Nested topic\u003c/title>\n    \u003cshortdesc>The child can be published on its own page.\u003c/shortdesc>\n    \u003cprolog>\u003cauthor>The tutorial team\u003c/author>\u003cmetadata>\u003ckeywords>\u003ckeyword>chunking\u003c/keyword>\u003c/keywords>\u003c/metadata>\u003c/prolog>\n    \u003crefbody>\u003csection>\u003cp>Check the generated parent and child links.\u003c/p>\u003c/section>\u003c/refbody>\n  \u003c/reference>\n\u003c/reference>"} lang="xml" title="examples/chunking/topics/nested.dita" />
      <CodeBlock code={"\u003c?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n\u003c!DOCTYPE map PUBLIC \"-//OASIS//DTD DITA Map//EN\" \"map.dtd\">\n\u003cmap>\n  \u003ctitle>Chunking demonstration\u003c/title>\n  \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/nested.dita\"/>\n\u003c/map>"} lang="xml" title="examples/chunking/combined.ditamap" />
      <CodeBlock code={"\u003c?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n\u003c!DOCTYPE map PUBLIC \"-//OASIS//DTD DITA Map//EN\" \"map.dtd\">\n\u003cmap>\n  \u003ctitle>Chunking demonstration\u003c/title>\n  \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/nested.dita\" chunk=\"by-topic\"/>\n\u003c/map>"} lang="xml" title="examples/chunking/split.ditamap" />
      <p>Run both builds from the project root:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"dita --input=examples/chunking/combined.ditamap --format=html5 --output=out/chunk-combined --nav-toc=full\ndita --input=examples/chunking/split.ditamap --format=html5 --output=out/chunk-split --nav-toc=full\npython3 scripts/check-output-links.py out/chunk-combined\npython3 scripts/check-output-links.py out/chunk-split"} lang="bash" />
      <p>Open each output's <code>index.html</code>. The combined version keeps the parent and child on one page. The split version should create a page for each topic. Follow the parent, child, and navigation links. Generated filenames can vary.</p>
      <p><strong>Warning:</strong> The previous effects example produced broken generated links with DITA-OT 4.3.5. Nested topics with <code>chunk="by-topic"</code> are valid DITA. The separate example preserves that lesson but does not guarantee that a processor will handle every chunking case correctly. Record the results for your version and transformation, and check generated links before publishing.</p>
      <h2 id="check-the-guide" class="group scroll-mt-20">Check the guide<a href="#check-the-guide" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <p>Run <code>scripts/check-stage.sh</code>, build the production deliverables, and run the output-link checker. Record remaining <a href="/dogsbay-xml-dita-tutorial-docs/reference/known-output-issues">known output issues</a> separately from the chunking experiment.</p>
      <p>Check that the effects and presets pages have stable filenames, the merged introduction links resolve, and the beginner formats page uses its alternate name. <code>outputclass="compact"</code> on the effects table supplies a CSS class; a stylesheet must define its visual effect.</p>
      <h2 id="what-you-learned" class="group scroll-mt-20">What you learned<a href="#what-you-learned" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <ul>
      <li><code>to-content</code> combines topics into an output document.</li>
      <li><code>by-topic</code> splits nested topics; inspect generated links as well as pages.</li>
      <li><code>copy-to</code> assigns an alternate output filename in a map.</li>
      <li>Print, navigation, and search attributes control different output features.</li>
      <li><code>topicset</code> and <code>topicsetref</code> reuse map branches.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2 id="next-lesson" class="group scroll-mt-20">Next lesson<a href="#next-lesson" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
